<title>INDIA: India's Andhra water corp plans 1.0 bln rupee bond.</title>
<headline>India's Andhra water corp plans 1.0 bln rupee bond.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Andhra Pradesh Water Resources Development Corporation (APWRDC) plans to privately place a 1.0-billion-rupee seven-year bond issue at 15.5 percent interest, arranger SBI Capital Markets Ltd said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The salient features of the bonds are as follows:</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Instrument	     Secured, Redeemable Non-Convertible Bonds</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Guarantee	     : Unconditionally and irrevocably</p>
<p>			    guaranteed by the Government of Andhra</p>
<p>			    Pradesh.</p>
<p>Credit Rating	 : A-(So) from Crisil.</p>
<p>			    (A Minus Structured Obligation).</p>
<p>Issue Size	    : 1,000 million with an option to retain</p>
<p>			    oversubscription.</p>
<p>Tenor		   : 7 years.</p>
<p>Call/Put Option     : At the end of 5 years.</p>
<p>Redemption	    : At par at the end of sixth and seven years</p>
<p>			    in equal instalments.</p>
<p>Face Value	    : Rs.100,000 per bond.</p>
<p>Minimum Application : 1 bond.</p>
<p>Upfront Discount    :  50 million		    - 0.5%</p>
<p>			    50 million to  100 million - 1%</p>
<p>			     100 million		   - 1.5%</p>
<p>Yield to Investors  : Maturity	   Put/Call</p>
<p>(Annualised)</p>
<p>Discount : 0.5%	  16.24%	     16.26%</p>
<p>	   : 1.0%	  16.37%	     16.42%</p>
<p>	   : 1.5%	  16.51%	     16.58%</p>
<p>Who can apply	 : Banks, FIs, Insurance Cos, Corporates,</p>
<p>			    FIIs, Co-op Banks etc.</p>
<p>Contacts		: Smita/Atul/Harsh/Piya/Ashish/Nihar at</p>
<p>			    2189166/2184510/2152260/2188332 (Fax)</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
